// data.js — WorkoutApp exercise & warm-up database
// Source of truth: WorkoutApp_Design_Spec_v2.md, sections 30-35 (exercises) and 8 (warm-up)
//
// Exercise.type: 'REPS' | 'TIME' | 'MAX'
//   REPS -> target is a number (fixed) or [min, max] (range, e.g. Good Morning)
//   TIME -> target is a duration in seconds
//   MAX  -> target is null, shown as "MAX CLEAN REPS", user enters actual count
// Exercise.image (optional): a data: URI (base64-embedded PNG/SVG), not a file
// path — embedded directly so the app has zero external file dependencies and
// can never show a broken-image icon regardless of how these files get copied
// around. .png ones are cropped from the user's own reference chart; .svg ones
// are simple hand-drawn stand-ins (lower fidelity, same dark/line-art palette)
// for exercises the chart didn't cover. A few secondary warm-up moves (Wrist
// Joint Warm-up, Dead Hang, Scapular Retraction/Pull) still have none.
//
// Legs A/B: resolved — the leg-specific portion is 3 exercises (Squats,
// Bulgarian Split Squats, Calf Raises), same for both A and B; Core still
// differs between A and B per the original spec (sections 32/35).
//
// ASSUMPTION (flagged, needs confirmation): "Pike Push-ups", "Pull-ups" and
// "Wide Pull-ups" in the B-day variants are listed in the spec with only a
// set count and no rep number (unlike their A-day versions, which do have a
// rep target). They are coded here as MAX type, matching the one exercise in
// the spec that is explicitly labeled that way (Archer Push-up Progression).
// This is a best-effort inference, not a spec change — confirm or correct.

